---
// PORTABLE: canonical copy - ncs-astro-sanity-starter is the library of record for this file
/* ============================================================================
   Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon
   ============================================================================
   Foundation, edit with care.

   Cookieless, privacy-friendly page views and Web Vitals. Nothing is stored on
   the visitor's device, so this needs no cookie banner and no consent gate.

   Rendered by Analytics.astro, and only when PUBLIC_CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN is set.
   This file owns the tag; Analytics.astro owns the condition.

   Setup, once per site:
     1. Cloudflare dashboard, Analytics and Logs, Web Analytics, Add a site.
     2. Cloudflare returns a token, a plain hex string.
     3. Put it in PUBLIC_CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN locally, and as a build variable on
        the deploy.
     4. Rebuild. The value is inlined at build time because these pages are
        prerendered, so a runtime variable will not do.

   This one IS printed as a literal tag, unlike its GA4 sibling. Cloudflare
   serves the beacon from its own edge on the same zone, so the Zaraz rewriting
   problem that forces the runtime-element trick for googletagmanager does not
   apply here.

   NO SUBRESOURCE INTEGRITY HASH ON PURPOSE, on this tag or on the GA4 loader.
   A linter will suggest one. Both vendors ship rolling builds behind a stable
   URL, so a pinned hash starts failing the moment the vendor updates, and a
   failed integrity check does not degrade: the browser refuses the script and
   analytics goes silently dead, which is the exact failure this whole card
   exists to prevent. Neither script is same-origin, so both are already
   covered by whatever the site's Content-Security-Policy allows.
   ============================================================================ */

interface Props {
  /** The Cloudflare Web Analytics site token (a hex string). */
  token: string;
}

const { token } = Astro.props;
---

<script
  defer
  src="https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js"
  data-cf-beacon={`{"token": "${token}"}`}></script>
